course: dictionary
lesson: 12676
title: Distorted: bent out of shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Distorted comes from the verb distort, which means to twist or change something so it no longer looks or sounds the way it really is. «The fairground mirror made my face look long and wobbly, so it was a distorted reflection.» The clues are the mirror and the wobbly face, so distorted means changed out of its normal shape.
explain: Sounds and pictures can be distorted too. «The phone call was crackly and distorted, so I could hardly hear Gran.» Crackly and hard to hear tells you the sound was changed and no longer clear. Ask yourself: is this different from how it really is?
explain: Facts can be distorted as well. «The advert used distorted facts and left out the bad news.» Here the facts were changed so that people get a false idea. This is why it is important to check information before you believe it.
fact: Distorted means twisted or changed out of its normal shape.
fact: A sound or picture that is distorted is unclear or not true to the original.
fact: «Distorted facts» means facts changed so they give a false idea.
fact: In science, water, lenses and curved mirrors can make distorted images.
fact: Distort is the verb, and distorted is its past form, which can also be used as an adjective.
exercise: «The bent spoon in the glass of water looked distorted.» What does distorted mean here? | Quiet and still | Shiny and new | Very cold | *Twisted or changed out of its normal shape
exercise: «The radio gave a crackly, distorted sound.» What does a distorted sound mean? | Louder and clearer than before | Very quiet, like a whisper | *Changed so it is unclear and not like the original | A sound made by a bird
exercise: «The leaflet used distorted facts to make the shop look better.» What is the problem with distorted facts? | *They are changed so they give a false idea | They are the correct facts, checked by everyone | They are facts about the weather | They are too long to read
test: Which of these is a distorted reflection? | A clear picture of the lake in still water | *A wobbly, stretched image in a curved mirror | A photo taken on a sunny day | A reflection in a flat window
test: Mia says distorted means the same as clear. Why is she wrong? | *Distorted means changed so it is no longer clear or true | Distorted means loud | Distorted means very clear and bright | Distorted means the same as new
exam: Why might someone share distorted facts? | To help people see the truth | To make a story shorter | *To give people a false idea | To be kind to their friends
